      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="how-we-chose" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. How We Chose These Watches</h2>
<p>
            We have not tested these watches on a treadmill, and nothing on this page should be
            read as if we had. Running watches change every year, so we started by confirming the
            current models on each maker's own store on 15 October 2026. Several familiar names are
            no longer the newest model: Garmin's newest Forerunners are the 70 and 170, launched in
            May 2026, alongside the 570 and 970; COROS sells the PACE 4; Apple's current models
            are the Series 12, the Ultra 4 and the SE 3; Polar's newest watch is the Street X; and
            Suunto now sells the Run alongside the newer Run 2 and Race 3S.
          </p>
          <p>
            For each candidate we checked four things against the maker's own product page, help
            centre or user manual: a treadmill or indoor run mode; a way to correct the distance
            after a treadmill run; foot pod pairing; and a direct connection to the treadmill
            through Apple GymKit or the Bluetooth FTMS standard. Prices and specifications were then
            cross-checked against independent review coverage. Where we could not open a maker's
            manual for a specific model, we say so on the card.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some strong watches were left out. The Garmin Forerunner 570 sits between our two
            Garmin picks and suits anyone who wants the 970's display and training features for
            less. The Suunto Run 2 and Race 3S were released recently enough that we could not yet
            cross-check their treadmill features and prices against independent sources, and the
            Polar Vantage M3 had no independent price we could confirm. The Apple Watch Ultra 4 and
            SE 3 behave the same way on a treadmill as the Series 12, so we list one Apple model and
            describe the others. One curiosity: the Zwift-branded watch launched in 2026 is a
            mechanical wristwatch with no electronics, so it plays no part here.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Safety check.</strong> We searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's
            recall database for Garmin, Apple, COROS, Polar and Suunto. We found no recall or
            warning for any watch on this page; the only Suunto entries concern diving equipment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="treadmill-features" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">4. What a Watch Can and Cannot Do on a Treadmill</h2>
<p>
            Without GPS, a watch has three ways to know your speed indoors: estimate it from your
            wrist and cadence, read it from a sensor on your shoe or chest, or receive it from the
            treadmill itself. The table shows which routes each pick documents.
          </p>
